  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound of {死|し} (death) + {滅|めつ} (destroy, extinguish). Often used in scientific contexts to describe the complete elimination of microorganisms, cells, or species. Also used figuratively for civilizations or traditions. Commonly used as a suru verb ({死滅|しめつ}する).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {細菌|さいきん}が{死滅|しめつ}する (bacteria die off)\n- {完全|かんぜん}に{死滅|しめつ}する (to be completely destroyed)\n- {死滅|しめつ}させる (to kill off, to destroy)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {絶滅|ぜつめつ}: extinction — typically used for species dying out completely\n- {消滅|しょうめつ}: disappearance, extinction — broader term for things ceasing to exist\n- {殺菌|さっきん}: sterilization — the deliberate act of killing bacteria",
